{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"LEAF 15f2 washedup-ropeable-hammerkop — phases 4a-4d.\n\n4b RED-FIRST, 22 tests (4 visible happy-path + 18 held out). Skeleton tests/_subprocess_isolation.py\nso RED lands on assertions. RESULT 12 FAILED / 10 passed.\nFailures all right-reason: 'assert hazard in []' x5 (the five hazard shapes), 'assert undecidable in\n[]' (the report-not-fail class), blank/bare marker x3, guard not wired into conftest, no UsageError\non the guard path, and the findings-shape test.\nFIXED ONE WRONG-REASON RED IN MY OWN TEST: the UsageError test crashed with\n'ValueError: substring not found' instead of asserting, because it indexed conftest text for a\nsubstring that does not exist yet. Now asserts presence first. A test that dies rather than fails\nproves nothing about its assertion.\nThe 10 passing are all ACCEPT-shape cases (asyncio.run not a spawn, locally-defined run, os.environ\nenv, subprocess_env helper, nested-pytest funnel, fixture cwd, tmp_path positional) which an\nempty-returning stub cannot fail; they get teeth from the mutation step.\n\nORACLE WEIGHTS THE FALSE-POSITIVE DIRECTION AS HEAVILY AS THE TRUE-POSITIVE ONE, deliberately: the\ncensus is 866 spawn sites of which ~841 are already legitimate and only ~26 are hazards, so a guard\nthat fails what it cannot prove safe would redden 42 files on introduction and simply get reverted.\nThe ~58 env=<bare variable> sites must be REPORTED as undecidable, never failed. Included a live-tier\ntest asserting no unmarked hazard remains, with the byte pre-filter (435 of 1261 files) so collection\ncost stays bounded.\n\n4c HELD OUT to job tmp. 4d DISPATCHED with the census, the three-way classification, the\nUsageError-not-pytest.fail precedent and its rationale, the nested-pytest exemption, the\nmandatory-reason rule (--strict-markers validates the NAME only), and the pre-filter requirement.\nTold it to report if the census numbers do not match what it measures rather than quietly\nreconciling them."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788319842305386001,"uuid":"84a35b43-1c79-4639-a44b-8c28cd3e96d5"}